IMPORT prelude

-- Urban Redevelopment Authority Act 1989 (Singapore) -- where the Authority meets a person or business: declaring an urban
-- redevelopment area (s 8), ex gratia payments (s 11), entry upon land and buildings (s 16), the penalties regulations may carry
-- (s 17(3)), the Authority's symbol (s 43), statistical notices, their service and the offence of not answering (s 44, 44A), the
-- secrecy of what is collected (s 45), obstruction (s 46), Public Prosecutor's consent (s 48), no liability for errors in paid
-- information (s 49), officers of a body corporate (s 50), composition (s 51A), and the quorum of the Authority (First Schedule
-- para 11(2)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 1 July 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/URAA1989.txt. The cover says the revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including
-- 1 December 2021"; the latest amendment annotated in the body is Act 15 of 2026, in force 1 July 2026 (s 6(i), (ia), (la), the
-- Authority's functions, not encoded).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0225 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. The Act is mostly constitutional (it sets up the Authority); the provisions a person or business meets are
-- the ones listed above, and they are encoded nearly whole.
--
-- Not encoded: the Authority's functions and powers (ss 6, 7, Second Schedule) beyond their mention here; Minister's directions,
-- projects, committees, delegation, standing orders (ss 9, 10, 12-15); staff (ss 18-20); finance (ss 22-29, Third Schedule); the
-- 1989 transfer of assets and employees (ss 30-40, Fourth Schedule); sale of developed land and registration of assurances
-- (ss 41, 42); conduct of prosecutions (s 47); fines paid to the Authority (s 51); the Minister's exemption power (s 52); and the
-- First Schedule beyond the quorum. The planning control most people associate with URA is in the Planning Act 1998, not here.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Urban Redevelopment Authority Act 1989 -- powers that reach the public`

§§ `8 -- declaring an urban redevelopment area`

-- s 8(1): the Authority "may, with the approval of the Minister, by notification in the Gazette declare an area ... to be an urban
-- redevelopment area". (2): the declaration "must contain" (a) the town subdivision or mukim, (b) the lot number, approximate area
-- and identifying particulars, (c) "if a plan of the area has been made, the place and time where and when the plan may be
-- inspected". (3): it "must state that such area may be acquired by the Government within 3 years from the date of the notification
-- in the Gazette or within such extended period as the President may think fit". (4): on publication the area "is deemed to be" an
-- urban redevelopment area.
GIVEN `the Minister approved` IS A BOOLEAN, `it was notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it names the subdivision or mukim and the lot` IS A BOOLEAN, `a plan has been made` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it says where and when the plan may be inspected` IS A BOOLEAN, `it states the acquisition period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the declaration is in the form the Act requires` IF
        `the Minister approved`
    AND `it was notified in the Gazette`
    AND `it names the subdivision or mukim and the lot`
    AND ((NOT `a plan has been made`) OR `it says where and when the plan may be inspected`)
    AND `it states the acquisition period`

-- The acquisition period stated under s 8(3), counted in months from the Gazette notification. An extension is whatever period
-- "the President may think fit" (0 if none). The Act states the period; it does not itself say what happens after it lapses.
GIVEN `months since the notification` IS A NUMBER, `months of extension by the President` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the stated acquisition period is still running` IF
    `months since the notification` AT MOST 36 PLUS `months of extension by the President`

§§ `11 -- ex gratia payments`

-- s 11: the Authority "may, with the approval of the Minister, make an ex gratia payment to a person sustaining damage by reason of
-- the exercise of one or more of the powers vested in the Authority or its employees under and by virtue of this Act". The word is
-- "may": the Act gives the person no entitlement, only the possibility.
GIVEN `the damage was caused by the exercise of a power under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister approves` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority may make an ex gratia payment` IF
    `the damage was caused by the exercise of a power under the Act` AND `the Minister approves`

§§ `16 -- entry upon land and buildings`

-- s 16(1): the Authority may "by its employees, agents or contractors, enter at all reasonable hours in the day into and upon a
-- building or land for the purpose of (a) making any survey or inspection; and (b) executing work authorised by this Act", without
-- being liable to legal proceedings. (2): they "must not enter into a building in actual occupation without the consent of the
-- occupier of the building or without 6 hours' previous notice to the occupier".
GIVEN `the purpose is a survey, inspection or authorised work` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is at a reasonable hour in the day` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the building is in actual occupation` IS A BOOLEAN, `the occupier consented` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `hours of notice given to the occupier` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the entry is authorised by section 16` IF
        `the purpose is a survey, inspection or authorised work`
    AND `it is at a reasonable hour in the day`
    AND (    (NOT `the building is in actual occupation`)
         OR  `the occupier consented`
         OR  `hours of notice given to the occupier` AT LEAST 6)

§§ `17(3), 43, 44(7), 45(2), 46 -- maximum penalties`

-- s 17(3): regulations may make a contravention an offence with "a fine not exceeding the sum of $2,000 or imprisonment for a term
-- not exceeding 3 months or both" and, for a continuing offence, "a further fine not exceeding $500 for every day or part of a day
-- during which the offence continues after conviction". These are the most a regulation MAY prescribe, not penalties the Act
-- imposes itself.
-- s 43(2): using the Authority's symbol, or one so resembling it as to be likely to deceive, without permission -- $2,000 or 6 months.
-- s 44(7): refusing or neglecting a statistical notice, or wilfully furnishing false particulars -- $2,000 or 6 months.
-- s 45(2): disclosing protected information -- $2,000 or ONE YEAR.
-- s 46: obstructing or hindering an officer or agent of the Authority -- $2,000 or 3 months.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `misusing the Authority's symbol`
    `refusing or neglecting a statistical notice`
    `furnishing false statistical particulars`
    `disclosing protected information`
    `obstructing an officer of the Authority`
    `contravening regulations under section 17`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine in dollars` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `misusing the Authority's symbol` THEN 2000
    WHEN `refusing or neglecting a statistical notice` THEN 2000
    WHEN `furnishing false statistical particulars` THEN 2000
    WHEN `disclosing protected information` THEN 2000
    WHEN `obstructing an officer of the Authority` THEN 2000
    WHEN `contravening regulations under section 17` THEN 2000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `misusing the Authority's symbol` THEN 6
    WHEN `refusing or neglecting a statistical notice` THEN 6
    WHEN `furnishing false statistical particulars` THEN 6
    WHEN `disclosing protected information` THEN 12
    WHEN `obstructing an officer of the Authority` THEN 3
    WHEN `contravening regulations under section 17` THEN 3

-- "every day or part of a day": a part day counts as a day, so the count passed in is whole days, part days rounded up.
GIVEN `days or part days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most a regulation may prescribe for a continuing offence` MEANS
    2000 PLUS 500 TIMES `days or part days continuing after conviction`

§§ `44 -- statistical notices`

-- s 44(1): the Authority "may, for the purpose of obtaining statistical information, by notice require any person to furnish ...
-- within such period as is specified in the notice, all such particulars or information ... as are within the person's knowledge or
-- in the person's custody or under the person's control".
-- (8): nothing in s 44 authorises requiring the Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore to furnish information "obtained in the
-- performance of any of its functions", or the Jurong Town Corporation to furnish information obtained under a notice under s 35A of
-- the JTC Act. That route is s 44A instead: a written requirement for statistical purposes relating to property, which IRAS must
-- answer for information obtained administering property tax or stamp duties, and JTC for its s 35A information, within a time
-- agreed between them.
DECLARE Recipient IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a partnership`
    `a company or limited liability partnership`
    `the Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore`
    `the Jurong Town Corporation`

GIVEN `the recipient` IS A Recipient, `the information is within its knowledge, custody or control` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the information was got in IRAS's functions or under a JTC section 35A notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 44 notice can require the information` IF
        `the information is within its knowledge, custody or control`
    AND CONSIDER `the recipient`
        WHEN `the Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore` THEN NOT `the information was got in IRAS's functions or under a JTC section 35A notice`
        WHEN `the Jurong Town Corporation` THEN NOT `the information was got in IRAS's functions or under a JTC section 35A notice`
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 44(7): a person who "(a) wilfully refuses or without lawful excuse (the proof of which lies on the person) neglects to furnish
-- the particulars or information within the time specified in the notice; or (b) wilfully furnishes or causes to be furnished any
-- false particulars or information" is guilty of an offence. A lawful excuse answers neglect; the text gives it no part in a wilful
-- refusal.
GIVEN `a notice required it` IS A BOOLEAN, `furnished within the time specified` IS A BOOLEAN, `the failure was a wilful refusal` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the person proved a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `wilfully furnished false particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 44(7)` IF
        `a notice required it`
    AND (   ((NOT `furnished within the time specified`) AND (`the failure was a wilful refusal` OR (NOT `the person proved a lawful excuse`)))
         OR `wilfully furnished false particulars`)

§§ `44(2), (3), (6) -- how the notice may be served`

-- s 44(2)(a) individual: personally; leaving with an adult or registered post to residence; the same to place of business; affixing
-- at residence or business; email to the address given for service. (b) partnership: to a partner or secretary; leaving or
-- registered post to the place of business; fax to the place of business; email. (c) LLP or other body corporate: to the secretary,
-- manager or person in control; leaving or registered post to the registered office or principal place of business; fax; email.
-- There is no fax for an individual and no affixing for a firm or company. (3): delivery to an agent within Singapore is good for
-- anyone. (6): email service "may be effected only if the person gives as part of the person's address for service an email
-- address".
DECLARE Method IS ONE OF
    `personal delivery`
    `registered post`
    `affixing at the address`
    `fax`
    `email`
    `delivery to an agent in Singapore`

GIVEN `the person served` IS A Recipient, `the method` IS A Method, `an email address was given for service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the method is allowed` IF
    CONSIDER `the method`
    WHEN `personal delivery` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `registered post` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `delivery to an agent in Singapore` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `email` THEN `an email address was given for service`
    WHEN `affixing at the address` THEN
        CONSIDER `the person served`
        WHEN `an individual` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `fax` THEN
        CONSIDER `the person served`
        WHEN `an individual` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `44(5) -- when the notice is deemed served`

-- s 44(5)(a) registered post: "deemed to be duly served ... at the time it would, in the ordinary course of post, be delivered,
-- whether or not it is returned undelivered". (b) ordinary post: "on the day after the day on which it would, in the ordinary course
-- of post, be delivered" (though (2) lists no ordinary post). (c) fax: "on the day of transmission, if a notification ... of a
-- successful transmission to that fax number is received". (d) email: "at the time of entering the information system addressed to
-- the email address".
-- Days are numbered. The rule gives the deemed day, or -1 where (5) deems no service (a fax with no notification of success).
DECLARE PostalMethod IS ONE OF
    `by registered post`
    `by ordinary post`
    `by fax`
    `by email`

GIVEN `how it was sent` IS A PostalMethod, `day of ordinary delivery or transmission` IS A NUMBER,
      `a successful fax notification was received` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deemed day of service` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how it was sent`
    WHEN `by registered post` THEN `day of ordinary delivery or transmission`
    WHEN `by ordinary post` THEN `day of ordinary delivery or transmission` PLUS 1
    WHEN `by fax` THEN
        IF `a successful fax notification was received` THEN `day of ordinary delivery or transmission` ELSE -1
    WHEN `by email` THEN `day of ordinary delivery or transmission`

§§ `45 -- secrecy of what is collected`

-- s 45(1): a member, officer or employee "must not disclose" particulars obtained under s 44 or 44A unless (a) with the previous
-- written consent of the person who furnished them or to whom they relate; (b) as statistics which do not identify that person;
-- (c) to JTC on its request under s 35B of the JTC Act; (d) to the Chief Statistician under s 6 of the Statistics Act 1973 (where
-- not exempted under s 6(2)); (e) to another member, officer or employee carrying the Act into effect; (f) for proceedings for an
-- offence under s 44(7) or s 45, or a report of them; (g) if "already in the public domain". (2): contravention is an offence.
DECLARE Disclosure IS ONE OF
    `with the person's prior written consent`
    `as statistics that identify no one`
    `to JTC on its section 35B request`
    `to the Chief Statistician on direction`
    `to a colleague carrying out the Act`
    `for proceedings under section 44(7) or 45`
    `of information already public`
    `to a property agent who asked`
    `of one owner's figures to a newspaper`

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is permitted` IF
    CONSIDER `the disclosure`
    WHEN `to a property agent who asked` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `of one owner's figures to a newspaper` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `49 -- errors in information supplied for a fee`

-- s 49: where the Authority supplies information to the public "on payment of a prescribed fee", neither it nor its employees are
-- liable for loss "by reason of any error or omission of whatever nature appearing therein or however caused if made in good faith
-- and in the ordinary course of the discharge of the duties of such employees". The section is silent on information given free;
-- whether liability then lies is left to the general law (inference: s 49 simply does not apply).
GIVEN `supplied on payment of a prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN, `the error was made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in the ordinary course of duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 49 excludes liability for the error` IF
    `supplied on payment of a prescribed fee` AND `the error was made in good faith` AND `in the ordinary course of duty`

§§ `48, 50, 51A -- prosecution, officers of a body corporate, composition`

-- s 48: "No court is to try an offence under this Act or any regulations made under this Act except with the consent of the Public
-- Prosecutor."
-- s 50: where a body corporate commits an offence "and is proved to have been committed with the consent or connivance of or to be
-- attributable to an act or default on the part of" a director, manager, secretary or similar officer (or one purporting to act as
-- such), he or she "as well as the body corporate" is guilty. The burden is on the prosecution: there is no due-diligence defence to
-- prove.
GIVEN `the body corporate committed the offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person is or purports to be a director, manager or secretary` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `consent, connivance, act or default of the person is proved` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Public Prosecutor consented to trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer can be tried for the offence` IF
        `the body corporate committed the offence`
    AND `the person is or purports to be a director, manager or secretary`
    AND `consent, connivance, act or default of the person is proved`
    AND `the Public Prosecutor consented to trial`

-- s 51A(1): the Authority "may compound any offence ... that is prescribed as a compoundable offence by collecting from a person
-- reasonably suspected of having committed the offence a sum not exceeding $1,000". (2): on payment "no further proceedings are to
-- be taken".
GIVEN `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `the sum collected in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence may be compounded for that sum` IF
    `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` AND `the sum collected in dollars` AT MOST 1000

§§ `First Schedule para 11(2) -- quorum`

-- "The quorum at every meeting of the Authority is one-third of the total number of members or 3 members, whichever is the higher."
-- s 4(1): a Chairperson and "not less than 4 and not more than 12 other members". Read as: present members must be at least
-- one-third of the total (no rounding needed: compare 3 times present with total) and at least 3.
GIVEN `members present` IS A NUMBER, `total members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a quorum` IF
    `members present` TIMES 3 AT LEAST `total members` AND `members present` AT LEAST 3
